\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Miyazawa, Hayami Mtg Leaves  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt Disapponted \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum \par \uc2 934 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 12:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--In an unusual move, Japan's finance minister and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor met in a hotel Thursday to discuss the recent sharp strengthening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But when it became clear that they'd done little else but talk in their meeting, the dollar plunged to its intraday low against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, who called the meeting, said he and Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami "had an important exchange of opinion, and decided to continue to have such exchanges and to deal with the current situation." \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa added, "I said that the recent yen strengthening has been rapid, and the Bank of Japan Governor agreed." \par \par \uc2  The meeting came amid mounting concern in Tokyo regarding the surging yen. Officials have become increasingly vehement in warning about the harm that can come from the yen's sudden rise, which has pushed the dollar down to Y104.15 from levels above Y120 as recently as mid-July. \par \par \uc2  News that Miyazawa was to meet with Hayami was enough to push the dollar to an intraday high of Y105.55 Thursday. When the two men failed to announce any new, concrete steps to halt the yen's advance, the dollar plunged to a low of Y103.77. \par \par \uc2  The two men met after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier revealed that its top financial diplomat, Vice Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda, would visit the U.S. to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taken together, the two events appeared to represent a new stage in\par Japan's efforts to tackle the strong yen. But they also underscored the\par difficulties the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is having in convincing the U.S.\par and other key players to join its efforts to stop the yen's rise.\par -\par          Intl Pleas Expected To Go Unheeded\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the ministry's pleas for foreign help are likely to fall\par on deaf ears for now, opening the way for a dollar drop to below\par Y100.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I doubt that (the U.S. and Japan) will be able to reach an agreement\par right away," said Taisuke Tanaka, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Credit\par Suisse First Boston in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For one thing, U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers and other top\par U.S. officials have expressed little concern about the yen's strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And although analysts blame the weak dollar as one factor behind the\par drop in U.S. stock and bond prices in the last couple of sessions, those\par markets haven't weakened to an extent that would alarm U.S. authorities,\par the analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Summers has made it pretty clear what his policy is," Tanaka said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although Summers has said repeatedly a strong dollar is in U.S.\par interests, he has also suggested \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  isn't the right way to\par assure a strong local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "What's right is not to seek to manage the markets, but instead to\par concentrate on building the right fundamentals for our economy," he said\par Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Miyazawa told reporters after his meeting with Hayami that while he\par and the BOJ Governor would explain Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stance to\par counterparts of the Group of Seven industrialized nations at a meeting\par in Washington later this month, he couldn't predict how their G7\par partners would respond to the explanation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said one factor that could prompt G7 partners to agree to\par coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be a protracted fall in Japanese stock\par prices. The Nikkei average of 225 Tokyo shares plunged 485.63 to close\par at 17,291.59 Thursday, the second straight session of falls.\par -\par         Threat To Recovery Could Compel Action\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. might give the go-ahead to coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if "the\par drop in stocks sours \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economic recovery hopes, and that in turn\par begins to hurt the world economy," Tanaka said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The prospect that the rising yen might derail the economic recovery\par prompted other top Tokyo officials to call for aggressive action in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Not just investors, but also the Japanese people will suffer" if the\par yen keeps rising, said Hiromu Nonaka, Japan's chief cabinet secretary.\par "I hope monetary authorities will take drastic measures" to counteract\par the move, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Such remarks come as Japanese officials and analysts call on the BOJ\par to ease monetary policy further to help cap the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One of the proposals gaining \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently is for the BOJ to leave\par the yen funds it sold during \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unsterilized in the\par money market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, analysts said that a move not to sterilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par funds would make little difference for monetary conditions or the yen's\par value, since the BOJ is already flooding the money market with extra\par funds. But the BOJ is likely to continue to feel pressure to take such a\par step.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's almost no meaning (in conducting unsterilized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ),\par but the market doesn't understand that," Tanaka said. The BOJ will have\par its next chance to leave funds unsterilized in the market Friday, the\par day the yen it sold during Tuesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  settles.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Miyazawa said after his meeting with Hayami that the two discussed the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy, but he said he didn't tell Hayami that\par the BOJ should leave \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds unsterilized. Hayami for his\par part stressed that the BOJ isn't prepared to change its current easy\par policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The zero interest rate policy is already more than sufficient as a\par monetary easing step," Hayami said.\par    -By Kenneth McCallum; 813-5255-2938; kmccallum@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1052GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4203 55128 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9g06tm5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
