\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  To Ask U.S., Europe For Joint  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  - Nikkei \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 01:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei)--Minister of Finance Kiichi Miyazawa Thursday evening agreed with Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami to ask U.S. and European monetary authorities to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the yen's recent steep rise, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported in its Friday morning edition, citing sources close to the matter. \par \par \uc2  The two officials agreed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's single-handed \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have had only a limited effect on restraining the yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters after the meeting, Miyazawa said, "It is of the utmost importance to notify those concerned in New York and Washington that the BOJ governor and I share the view" on this matter. He also indicated his intention to explain to U.S. and European monetary authorities that the yen's rapid appreciation will nip Japan's budding economic recovery, and he will seek their cooperation in curbing the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's attention will now shift to whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  can line up support for joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise ahead of a meeting of finance ministers and central bankers from the Group of Seven industrialized nations, which is due to open in Washington on Sept. 25. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the BOJ governor brushed aside Miyazawa's indirect request for so-called "unsterilized" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to implement a further monetary easing, the sources said. Hayami said, "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is injecting more than enough liquidity into the market with its zero-interest policy." \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-09-99 \par \par \uc2  2329GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9g06tcg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
