\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW/Ex-MOF Oba -2: Joint  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  "One Option" \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 09:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A top Japanese monetary official will probably talk this week with his counterparts from the U.S. Treasury about the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Tomomitsu Oba, president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Center for International Finance. \par \par \uc2  A former vice finance minister for international affairs, Oba said that Haruhiko Kuroda, the current vice minister for international affairs at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may very well bring up the issue of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with U.S. Treasury officials when he visits Washington D.C. later Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "This is probably why (Finance Minister Kiichi) Miyazawa sent Kuroda to the U.S.," Oba said in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  Oba said that there's a good chance that Kuroda will ask how the U.S. perceives the recent sharp fall of the dollar against the yen and seek cooperation from his counterparts on jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to put a halt to the dollar's slide. \par \par \uc2  "Based on my experience, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually emphasizes coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the U.S. normally emphasizes coordinated policies including \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japan may try to get the U.S.'s agreement on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for a change in Japanese fiscal or monetary policies," Oba said. \par \par \uc2  Oba said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  solely and should also consider U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as "one option" to stem the dollar's plunge against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Oba was speaking as the dollar traded around Y104.90 in Tokyo late Thursday. As recently as mid-July, the dollar was above Y120. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 16-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0736GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9g06t2w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
