\par\par \b \uc2  Key points of Miyazawa-Hayami meeting. \b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 11:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The following are key points of a meeting between Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami at a Tokyo hotel on Thursday: \par \par \uc2  * The meeting was held after the yen surged to around 103.25 to the dollar, a 45-month high, on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  * The meeting comes a little over a week before Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers meet in Washington. \par \par \uc2  * Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan's top financial diplomat, is in Washington to talk with his counterparts from other nations and to "analyse" Japan's situation. \par \par \uc2  * Miyazawa said: "We had a very positive discussion. We talked about recent rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and the need to have other nations understand Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation." \par \par \uc2  * "The most important thing we discussed was how the BOJ governor and I think, and how to present and match our views in New York and Washington to related parties," Miyazawa told reporters after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  * Hayami said he exchanged views with Miyazawa on the impact of the yen's recent rise on Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  * Hayami said: "The MOF and the BOJ agreed to keep close contact on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and to tackle the situation." \par \par \uc2  * Miyazawa did not announce any new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures or indicate any shift in policy. The issue of whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should stop "sterilising" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after selling yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market did not come up, Miyazawa said. \par \par \uc2  * Miyazawa said the two discussed monetary policy, but he did not elaborate on what was said. \par \par \uc2  * Hayami said he and Miyazawa did not discuss specific monetary policy issues, such as further easing monetary policy or not sterilising \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  * Hayami said: "The BOJ's current virtually zero interest rate policy is more than sufficient to provide ample funds in the money market." \par \par \uc2  * Regarding sterilisation, Hayami said: "We will not change current policy to sterilise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  * Miyazawa was accompanied by Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the ministry's International Bureau, which implements \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. He declined comment afterwards. \par \par \uc2  * Two key BOJ officials - International Department Director Eiji Hirano and Policy Planning Office Chief Manager Masayoshi Amamiya - were with Hayami. \par \par \uc2  * Miyazawa maintained his usual reticence over whether the G7 meeting in Washington would deal mainly with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues. \par \par \uc2  * Miyazawa flatly declined to comment on the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with other nations. \par \par \uc2  * Neither man commented on the state of Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  * The Miyazawa-Hayami meeting lasted about 45 minutes. \par \par \uc2  * The meeting, held on neutral turf at Tokyo's Palace Hotel, was initially taken by markets as a sign that Miyazawa wanted to pressure the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease its monetary policy. ((Ami Miyazaki and Reed Stevenson (813) 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00llw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
