\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Yen rally pauses on renewed BOJ fears. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 17:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The yen pared its gains against the dollar on Thursday, down around 1.5 percent from 3-1/2 year peaks set in the previous session, in choppy trade on renewed fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami met in Tokyo earlier in the day to discuss monetary policy, but announced no new measures to stem the yen's upward path, although they agreed they would respond to a drastic rise in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Concerns the BOJ may act in conjuction with other central banks were also highlighted after it was announced top Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda was in Washington to discuss recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions with officials from other nations. \par \par \uc2  "The market keeps wanting to take the yen higher, but you get pull backs with these sort of comments. Dollar/yen has been bouncing around quite a bit today," said Ryan Shea international economist, First Chicago. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone in the market is gearing themselves up for some expectation of either unilateral BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or more importantly bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the U.S." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 104.72/82 yen by 1452 GMT compared with 104.19/29 late in Europe on Wednesday. The dollar traded between 105.57 and 103.54 yen on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Gerard Lyons global head of treasury research at Standard Chartered Bank in London was looking for dollar/yen to breach the 100 yen level. \par \par \uc2  "The important thing is that the move on dollar/yen was justified on a number of factors (for instance) the improving economic picture in Japan and also a bit more uncertainty about events in the U.S.," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Having had such a big move it is natural for the markets to be wary of pushing the yen immediately stronger, particularly given the policy comments made by the Japanese." \par \par \uc2  Despite talk of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Lyons said it was unlikely to be successful. \par \par \uc2  "For \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have anything more than a transitory impact it would require the U.S. to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I don't see them wanting to," he said. \par \par \uc2  "If the U.S. did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  it would not help the euro/dollar rate and the Americans have to be sensitive to European needs as well as to Japanese needs." \par \par \uc2  The euro was last at 108.98/87 yen versus 108.19/29 late in Europe on Wednesday after tracking moves in euro/dollar. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro was at $1.0395/97 compared with an eight-week low of $1.0283 set on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Shea at First Chicago said there was scope for the euro to appreciate against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "One thing which may have been helping to keep it soft is that the ECB has been coming out with relatively optimistic comments on inflation," he said. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said in the Irish Times newspaper on Thursday that the inflation outlook was favourable and that interest rates were likely to remain low into next year. \par \par \uc2  "That seems to suggest interest rates will remain unchanged for the rest of the year, and that scaling back of interest rate expectations has helped take some of the sting out of the dollar's weakness in terms of the euro," Shea said. \par \par \uc2  From a U.S. perspective, he said the dollar remained under pressure. Uncertainty about whether or not the Federal Open Market Committee would leave U.S. interest rates unchanged for the rest of the year meant U.S. equity and Treasury markets were vulnerable to the downside. \par \par \uc2  "From an international perspective that means you probably want to get out of the dollar in general as a vehicle for investment," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The bearish dollar scenario remains intact but at the moment you are seeing it primarily in place against the yen." \par \par \uc2  ((London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00lkd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
