\par\par \b \uc2  Miyazawa says met Hayami to match views before G7. \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he met Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami on Thursday to match their opinions ahead of a Group of Seven financial meeting they will attend late this month. \par \par \uc2  "We exchanged views, that was the purpose of our meeting," Miyazawa told reporters after meeting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor for about 45 minutes at a Tokyo hotel. \par \par \uc2  "We also discussed recent market movements and their effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy." \par \par \uc2  Asked if the BOJ's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday was ineffective, Miyazawa said there was a need for other nations to better understand Japan's situation (with regard to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). \par \par \uc2  Asked if his view on the need for other countries to understand Japan's situation meant Japan was aiming for joint cooperation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the rising yen, he said it was best that he not comment on the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  When asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be one of the main topics at the Group of Seven finance ministers' meeting to be held around September 25, Miyazawa said: "There are still some days before that. I can't say." \par \par \uc2  "The most important thing we discussed was how the BOJ governor and I think, and how to present and match our views in New York and Washington to related parties," Miyazawa said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa responded affirmatively when asked if he and Hayami had discussed monetary policy issues. \par \par \uc2  "It was a good opportunity to discuss monetary policy under present conditions," Miyazawa said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa said they did not discuss the issue of whether the BOJ should leave its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised. ((Reed Stevenson and Ami Miyazaki (813) 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00ldk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
