\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar wins reprieve from recent yen attack. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 21:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The dollar won a reprieve from a recent onslaught by the Japanese yen on Thursday as jitters over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to tame Japan's soaring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resonated through the markets. \par \par \uc2  The market focused on talks in Washington between top Japanese Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda and U.S. Treasury officials, which markets speculated revolved around \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market conditions and possible joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Officials declined to detail an agenda for what they said were "routine" talks ahead of a broader meeting of finance officials scheduled for Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is exceptionally thin and very, very nervous," said John McCarthy, senior vice president at ING Barings. \par \par \uc2  The dollar whipped in tight ranges against the yen and Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for much of the U.S. session, making dealers reluctant to take on significant positions. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously there's concern (about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), and you witness this concern in the choppiness and the sharp and violent moves," McCarthy said. \par \par \uc2  But by late afternoon, already spotty dealing slowed to a trickle as New York braced for Hurricane Floyd's arrival and some financial markets closed shop early, although \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing remained open. \par \par \uc2  The yen gave up a small portion of its recent sharp gains, as dealers squared positions in anticipation of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , giving the dollar a reprieve and allowing it to hold above 3-1/2 year lows near 103 yen hit on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yen had jumped more than seven percent since September 9, when Japan released fresh strong growth data. \par \par \uc2  By 1500 EDT/1900 GMT, the dollar climbed to 105.15/25 yen from 104.14/24 in early U.S. dealing and from 104.66/76 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Despite recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, however, the market showed little response to comments from a senior IMF official, who said the IMF would discuss joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Japanese and G7 officials. \par \par \uc2  The market was also largely unmoved by a monthly report from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that warned that upward risks to price stability merit close attention. \par \par \uc2  But in its September report, the ECB also noted there are no immediate dangers to euro zone price stability, and increases in the euro zone Consumer Price Index are likely to level off below 2.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was barely changed against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the euro tightly orbited the $1.04 level. After heading into the U.S. session slightly lower at $1.0379/86 from $1.0405/10 late Wednesday, the euro bounced to $1.0403/08. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, a meeting between Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, plus the news of Kuroda's visit to Washington sparked the yen's sharp moves. \par \par \uc2  While the Japanese government says a rise in the yen is generally a sign of a welcome "buy Japan" mentality, it also fears the yen's recent sharp surge may smother the nascent recovery that has sparked the buying. \par \par \uc2  The dollar quickly jumped above 105 yen overnight when traders hoped the Miyazawa meeting would produce fresh tactics to tame yen strength. But when officials stopped short of suggesting a shift in policy, the yen regained the upper hand. \par \par \uc2  "What is yet to be seen is whether the U.S. Treasury or the G7 more broadly will support joint \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," analysts at BankBoston said. \par \par \uc2  As long as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to sterilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by effectively withdrawing the money it has pumped into the system through the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers predicted Washington's policy will remain hands off. \par \par \uc2  In other dealing, the British pound was not far from session highs at $1.6235/45 from $1.6163/73 in early New York trading and from $1.6140/50 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (( N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1607 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00hxq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
