\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar mixed at choppy U.S. midday, eyes on BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 20:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The dollar tread choppy trading waters at U.S. midday, inching up against the Japanese yen as dealers remained on guard for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to tame Japan's soaring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  News that top Japanese Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda was in Washington to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market conditions set the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on edge as talk of joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  swirled. \par \par \uc2  "The whole market is kind of thin and skittish at this point," said Grant Wilson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Mellon Bank. \par \par \uc2  "It's really whipping back and forth in the little ranges that we're making," Wilson said, adding traders were reluctant to take on significant positions. \par \par \uc2  The yen gave up a small portion of its recent sharp gains, as dealers squared positions in anticipation of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , giving the greenback a reprieve and allowing it to hold above 3-1/2 year lows near 103 yen hit on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yen had jumped over seven percent since September 9, when Japan released fresh strong growth data. \par \par \uc2  By 1300 EDT/1700 GMT, the dollar climbed to 105.00/10 yen from 104.14/24 in early U.S. dealing and from 104.66/76 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar was barely changed against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the euro tightly orbited the $1.04 level. After heading into the U.S. session slightly lower at $1.0379/86 from $1.0405/10 late Wednesday, the euro bounced to $1.0408/13. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters, however, the market showed little response to comments from a senior IMF official, who said the IMF would discuss joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Japanese and G7 officials. \par \par \uc2  Thin trading conditions would likely make for volatile price moves, and volumes could slow to a trickle as New York prepares for the arrival of Hurricane Floyd, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The fixed-income markets as well as some other exchanges closed early at 1300 EDT/1700 GMT, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing will remain open, and the New York Stock Exchange also planned to maintain regular trading hours. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, a meeting between Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, plus the news of Kuroda's visit to Washington sparked the yen's sharp moves. \par \par \uc2  While the Japanese government says a rise in the yen is generally a sign of a welcome "buy Japan" mentality, it also fears the yen's recent sharp surge may smother the nascent recovery that has sparked the buying. \par \par \uc2  The dollar quickly jumped above 105 yen overnight when traders hoped the Miyazawa meeting would produce fresh tactics to tame yen strength. But when officials stopped short of suggesting a shift in policy, the yen regained the upper hand. \par \par \uc2  "What is yet to be seen is whether the U.S. Treasury or the G7 more broadly will support joint \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," analysts at BankBoston said. \par \par \uc2  As long as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to sterilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by effectively withdrawing the money it has pumped into the system through the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers predicted Washington's policy will remain hands off. \par \par \uc2  In other dealing, the British pound climbed near its session highs to $1.6240/50 from $1.6163/73 in early New York trading and from $1.6140/50 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Elizabeth Lazarowitz, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1607)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00e8z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
