\par\par \b \uc2  Strong yen struts its stuff in Asia. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1999\par 08:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The yen showed little sign of running out of steam in Asian trade on Wednesday, climbing higher against the dollar and hitting fresh peaks against the euro in a volatile market thinned by a holiday in Japan. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there were no changes in the underlying factors with optimism about Japan's recovery and growing concern about the robustness of U.S. asset markets keeping the yen firm. \par \par \uc2  "The economic numbers that we've seen of late are positive for Japan. And coupled with the poor current account deficit numbers from the U.S., it will only mean a greater slide in dollar/yen," said Chin Loo Thio, strategist at Paribas. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. current account deficit rose to a record $80.67 billion in the second quarter, against a $68.65 billion deficit in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  Analysts in a Reuters poll had forecast on average a $78.9 billion deficit for the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  The release of strong U.S. retail sales data for August overnight stoked fears of another rate hike by the Federal Reserve. Dealers said the August Consumer Price Index, due at 1230 GMT, would now be even more keenly scrutinised. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 105.34/39 yen at 0600 GMT, against its New York close at 105.78/84. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen hit new lifetime lows throughout the morning and at 0600 GMT was quoted at 108.50/68. The euro was at $1.0309/11 against a New York close at $1.0356/58. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the drop in euro/yen was exaggerated by illiquid Asian markets, with spreads occasionally widening alarmingly beyond 40 ticks showing a marked reluctance to trade by some banks. But others continued to quote a five tick spread. \par \par \uc2  The market was also becoming increasingly gung-ho about the potential impact of any Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise after the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday failed to create more than a temporary dent. \par \par \uc2  "Their success has been very limited. If you look at yesterday's action, it didn't even go to 107.50," said Karl Broecker, head of treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttemberg in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "To give a clearer signal, they have to come up with unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and flood the market with liquidity. What they are doing currently is half-hearted and I think it is accelerating the trend," he told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  Steve Brice, treasury economist at Standard Chartered, said the yen would indeed weaken if the BOJ stopped sterilising its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or draining excess yen from the money market. \par \par \uc2  "But I don't think the BOJ would be happy to do that on an expansive basis," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consistently absorbed surplus yen funds after its dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and most analysts don't expect a shift in its stance. \par \par \uc2  There was also little likelihood of a joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as U.S. asset markets remained fairly stable, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The (U.S) is not concerned unless they experience a greater shake-up in their own financial markets. This is not the case right now. At 100 (yen to the dollar), it still may not be the case," said Thio at Paribas. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there'll be a big sell-off in US treasuries because of the lack of investment alternatives. Despite the fact that Asia's improving, you still have the Y2K risk," she added. \par \par \uc2  ((Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840;fax (65) 870-3787; email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9f00pfg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
