\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen set to power on vs dollar, euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 1,085 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1999\par 17:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The yen rose sharply against the dollar and euro on Wednesday and without Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check its gains, analysts see the yen pushing to 100 yen and beyond. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen fell to 3-1/2 year lows at 103.25 and euro/yen to life lows below 107 in Europe as yen bulls, fuelled by the prospect of a Japanese economic recovery, tested the nerve of the Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  "Momentum for dollar/yen is on the downside. The market is pushing the Bank of Japan into action," said Stephen Saywell, treasury analyst at Fuji Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market was nervous about 105, pushed it through and saw no reaction from the BOJ and became more aggressive and more confiedent that the BOJ wouldn't come in. We are now heading for 100 unless the BOJ comes in and does something about it." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 104.20/25 yen by 1430 GMT, having earlier fallen more than 2.5 percent to 103.25, its lowest since January 1996. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 107.89/93 yen having pared losses after hitting a life low at 106.84 earlier in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Since the release of Japanese gross domestic product data on September 9, which surprised the market by showing a second consecutive quarter of growth, dollar/yen has fallen by seven percent and euro/yen by nine percent. \par \par \uc2  "There is an element of panic in the market and it is all to do with Japanese investors who are concerned about postions abroad. If the authorities are seen as unable to do anything about it, it will exacerbate the situation, so at some stage something must be done," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  He said possible scenarios that might reverse the downward spiral in dollar/yen would be a correction on the Nikkei, joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between the BOJ and one or more of the other Group of Seven central banks or if the BOJ were to leave \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised. \par \par \uc2  So far, the BOJ has conducted a process known as sterilisation to soak up the excess liquidity in the money market resulting from its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The markets are pushing the BOJ for sterilisation," said Saywell at Fuji Bank. \par \par \uc2  "It might take something radical, a change of policy somehow, or even a change in stance at the BOJ for that to be done, but the market will need that type of symbolism to turn its sentiment away from the yen at the moment." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said for now joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely, given comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minster Kiichi Miyazawa on Tuesday that the yen's strength was a problem for Japan to address and that he did not expect it to be dicussed at the meeting of G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors on September 25. \par \par \uc2  The dollar took some comfort on Wednesday from benign U.S. inflation data which did much to allay inflation fears prompted by the release of stronger-than-expected U.S. August retails sales numbers followed by a record U.S. current account deficit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Headline August consumer price data was in line with expectations, up 0.3 percent and the core data rose 0.1 percent, compared with expectations of a 0.2 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  "The market has immediately unwound the risks that they had priced in yesterday of a rate hike at the October 5 meeting. The general view is now that the Fed could be on hold for the rest of the year," said Halpenny at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the euro was somewhat sidelined with little to distract the market from the yen's gains. \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly dipped to eight-week lows at $1.0287 after the U.S. data bouyed the dollar, but has since returned to the middle of the day's trading range and was last at $1.0381/83. \par \par \uc2  "People are talking about euro/dollar testing parity, but I don't see that at the moment. The (life) low is at $1.0104 and that is quite a long way away," said Fuji Bank's Saywell. ((London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  "The markets are pushing the BOJ for sterilisation," said Saywell at Fuji Bank. \par \par \uc2  "It might take something radical, a change of policy somehow, or even a change in stance at the BOJ for that to be done, but the market will need that type of symbolism to turn its sentiment away from the yen at the moment." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said for now joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely, given comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minster Kiichi Miyazawa on Tuesday that the yen's strength was a problem for Japan to address and that he did not expect it to be dicussed at the meeting of G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors on September 25. \par \par \uc2  The dollar took some comfort on Wednesday from benign U.S. inflation data which did much to allay inflation fears prompted by the release of stronger-than-expected U.S. August retails sales numbers followed by a record U.S. current account deficit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Headline August consumer price data was in line with expectations, up 0.3 percent and the core data rose 0.1 percent, compared with expectations of a 0.2 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  "The market has immediately unwound the risks that they had priced in yesterday of a rate hike at the October 5 meeting. The general view is now that the Fed could be on hold for the rest of the year," said Halpenny at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the euro was somewhat sidelined with little to distract the market from the yen's gains. \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly dipped to eight-week lows at $1.0287 after the U.S. data bouyed the dollar, but has since returned to the middle of the day's trading range and was last at $1.0381/83. \par \par \uc2  "People are talking about euro/dollar testing parity, but I don't see that at the moment. The (life) low is at $1.0104 and that is quite a long way away," said Fuji Bank's Saywell. ((London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9f00j1i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
