\par\par \b \uc2  EPA Sakaiya -3: Considering Future Monetary Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 05:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Turning to monetary policy, Sakaiya said that future policy, including that on long-term interest rates, will be closely considered within a framework of overall economic policy. However, he refused to comment on whether any changes would be made. \par \par \uc2  Asked about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should be sterilized or not, Sakaiya said that the Bank of Japan's choice whether or not to sterilize funds depended on the amount of funds in the money market at that time, saying that "it is a decision that must be made at the time (of action)," he said. \par \par \uc2  The problem of supplying funds to the market and that of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are two different things in principle, he said. \par \par \uc2  Asked about whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the yen's rise against the dollar, Sakaiya declined to comment except to say that "(\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is always on my mind, but it is something you should ask the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  about." \par \par \uc2  Commenting on Tuesday morning's cabinet meeting, Sakaiya said that "several" short-term economic policies were discussed but did not go into details. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0321GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9e06rm2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw18