\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Supports Dlr Downside But Little More \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 12:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Several rounds of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to give the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than a temporary lift, demonstrating the large amount of dollar-selling interest in the market. \par \par \uc2  After the dollar set a new 40-month low of Y106.00 and threatened to fall further, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began a buying spree that eventually cost it between $1 billion and $2 billion, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last Friday, Tuesday's action was ineffective in providing a sustained boost to the dollar, both because the scale was relatively small and because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost the advantage of surprise, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Still, some traders gave the BOJ credit for injecting just enough two-way risk into the market to keep the dollar from plunging. \par \par \uc2  Following Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar shot up by a yen to a high of Y107.15 but soon sank back below Y107.00. Late in the Asian day, the dollar was quoted around Y106.41. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been effective in slowing down the dollar's downward move, if that is their intention," said Kenneth Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa suggested in a news conference that Tokyo was aiming to stabilize market movements rather than reverse the trend toward a weaker dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I feel that recent moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have been rapid. It is our principle that we will act on excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves," Miyazawa said. \par \par \uc2  The yen's resilience in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflects steady investor appetite for Japanese assets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Overseas players such as U.S. funds and Middle Eastern names are buying yen for dollars in order to invest in Japanese assets, as Japan's economic fundamentals are improving while the U.S. economy has topped out and is slowing down," said a dealer at a Tokyo-based European bank who wished to remain anonymous. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, Japanese institutional investors are buying yen against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the dollar and the euro to either hedge or reduce their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated assets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Some investors are hedging their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure on their overseas assets, while others are repatriating yen from these assets ahead of half-year book-closing at the end of September," a dealer at a Japanese trust bank said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       Dollar Could Fall Further In Coming Months\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given this strong yen-buying interest from both foreign and Japanese\par players, the dollar could fall further in the coming months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Some market participants expect the dollar to drop to Y105 in the\par next one month," the European bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Deutsche Bank's Landon said the dollar could test support at Y99 some\par time in 1999, although in the short term the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could benefit\par from a brief short-covering rally. He said he expects the dollar to\par trade between Y106 and Y108 for the rest of the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some traders expressed surprise that the yen remained robust on\par Tuesday even after a senior policy maker seemed to hint at the\par possibility of further monetary easing. Economic Planning Agency chief\par Taichi Sakaiya said that future economic policy decisions could\par incorporate monetary steps.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although Sakaiya was somewhat vague in his remarks, he noted that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could change course in how it deals with excessive yen\par supply in the money market following yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Until now, the BOJ has consistently absorbed excess yen, thereby\par sterilizing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Sakaiya suggested the BOJ could shift\par tact.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As a rule, excessive fund supplies and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are separate\par issues. But if both issues arise at the same time, choosing not to\par sterilize \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is an option," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese bond prices rose on Sakaiya's remark and the yen eased\par momentarily. But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later bounced back.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the dollar will likely remain in its downtrend as long as\par U.S. officials remain cool to the idea of joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the\par BOJ.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. officials have consistently denied that joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is in\par the cards at this point. Most recently, President Bill Clinton's chief\par economic adviser Gene Sperling said Monday that the U.S. and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par wouldn't likely discuss coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when finance ministers\par from both nations meet in Washington later this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Landon noted that U.S.-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely based on\par comments from U.S. officials. "From everything the U.S. has been saying,\par it doesn't sound like they (U.S.) will join \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in joint\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Ron Harui (813-5255-2929;rharui@ap.org)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1027GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1135 4254 55128 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9e06q0p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
