\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ drains funds from its yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) has dashed speculation that it would use its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to pump more money into the banking system, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, analysts and traders. \par \par \uc2  Market sources said the BOJ had "sterilised" last Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by removing from circulation the estimated 217 billion yen ($2.05 billion) it spent to try to keep the yen from rising. \par \par \uc2  The government fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp rise could derail the economic recovery by making Japanese exports more expensive. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ removed the money through its daily money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tuesday, when settlements for Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came due, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At its regular 0020 GMT \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ left the money market with a surplus of 1.2 trillion yen (US$11.3 billion), slightly higher than the 1.0 trillion surplus left the previous day. That initially led some market participants to believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not sterilised Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , causing bond and euroyen futures to briefly rise. \par \par \uc2  Yet traders soon abandoned that belief as the view spread that the larger surplus had been left to counter a rise in the overnight interest rate and to meet a temporary increase in fund demand. \par \par \uc2  Still, many traders believe pressure is mounting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease credit as the yen has soared to a three-year high of 106 yen the dollar, up about 15 percent since this year's high of 124.75 yen hit on May 20 and from around 132 yen to the dollar a year ago. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ attempted to temper the yen's rise by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading again on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Hubert Neiss, Asia-Pacific director for the IMF, said in early September that the BOJ could check the yen's rise by more aggressively injecting liquidity into the money market through "unsterilised" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly rejected that option, though. \par \par \uc2  "We are already providing ample funding through other means," BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has consistently absorbed surplus yen funds after it bought an estimated $37.76 billion through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and July. \par \par \uc2  Hayami reiterated the BOJ's doubts about whether an unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more effective than the present monetary policy of pumping funds into the money market to guide the key overnight call rate essentially to zero. \par \par \uc2  Most Japan-based analysts don't expect the BOJ to alter that stance, especially to influence exchange rates, which it sees as lying outside its realm of responsibility. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ wants to draw a clear line between the BOJ's monetary policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, which is conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Kazuhiko Sano, chief strategist at Daiwa Securities SB Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  That view was echoed on Tuesday by Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya, who told a news conference: "In principle, (the BOJ) supplying funds to the money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should be considered separately." \par \par \uc2  He added, however, that unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained one option for the BOJ if monetary easing and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were needed at the same time. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the Japanese government may press the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to further loosen its credit grip flared after Sakaiya said monetary policy will be discussed as one aspect of its upcoming economic stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  ($=106.35 yen) \par \par \uc2  ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9e00o2v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
