\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen confidence eclipses dollar, euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 14:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The yen maintained its bullish stance on Tuesday around half a yen below a three-year high against the dollar and a record high against the euro set in the previous session. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight to sell yen for dollars had no lasting impact on dollar/yen which failed to sustain levels above 107 seen following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the fact that we had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight it hasn't done much good and I don't think anyone is really surprised. The yen is pushing aginst its highs," said David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "The same factors are driving the market as were yesterday and last week, we are just at slightly different levels." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was at 106.38/43 by 1042 GMT, off a high of 107.21 seen overnight and compared with a three-year low of 105.98 set on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said overnight he did not expect the G7 finance ministers meeting later in September to discuss joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that the yen's rise was fundamentally \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's problem. \par \par \uc2  "In a sense they shot themselves in the foot," said Coleman. "Miyazawa is effectively saying the U.S. and presumably G7 are not going to get involved and that takes away any fear the market might have had of a more coordinated approach to the yen issue." \par \par \uc2  Comments from a source from the economics department of one European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier on Tuesday backed up that view. \par \par \uc2  The source, who was attending a meeting of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance minstry officials at the Paris-based Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development, said he did not think the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to help Jpaan contain the yen's recent surge. \par \par \uc2  Michael Metcalfe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at NatWest Global Finanical Markets in London said the day's low at 106.03 was likely to be tested later in the session. \par \par \uc2  "We may even get through 106, especially as with a Japanese holiday tomorrow there may be a perception that the Bank of Japan won't be there," he said. \par \par \uc2  For the dollar, analysts said the main focus would be the U.S. August retail sales due at 1230 GMT and second quarter current account deficit data at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The current account could be watched closely," said CIBC's Coleman. "The dollar is in a downtrend, the market is in a mood to buy yen and sell dollars so any disappointment there would probably push the dollar lower." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen's buoyancy against the dollar was helping to keep pressure on the euro. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen was last at 110.14/50 after pulling back from an overnight high of 111.39 and compared with a life low of 109.53 set on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Some investors may be looking for alternatives to buy yen against and the euro good candidate given the economic fundamentals," said Coleman at CIBC. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0355/60 half a percentage point above the $1.0296 low set on Monday, the euro's lowest level in nearly eight weeks. \par \par \uc2  "Euro weakness is a function of two things; the euro/yen cross and comments from ECB members last week," said Metcalfe at NatWest GFM. \par \par \uc2  ECB board members Eugenio Domingo Solans and Sirrka Hamalainen said last week that euro stability was more important than euro strength. \par \par \uc2  Metcalfe said within the euro zone, inflation was starting to be looked at more closely. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the Spanish consumer price index showed inflation rose 2.4 percent year-on-year in August and the government raised its inflation forecast for 1999 to 2.4 percent from 1.8 percent previously. \par \par \uc2  "There is a possibility that interest rates may have to rise in Europe a little bit sooner than everyone thought. That would not be great for the recovery and is probably a slight negative for the euro, but not significantly so," said Metcalfe. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, good British retail price inflation data dented sterling's performance against the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  The August retail price index showed the underlying inflation rate rose 0.2 percent on the month and 2.1 percent on the year, and was the lowest since October 1994. The Bank of England has set a target for 2.5 percent for the underlying inflation rate. \par \par \uc2  The pound was last at $1.6014/24 compared with $1.6073/83 late on Monday in Europe. Sterling was less than one penny away from its life high of 63.79 pence against the euro set in June. \par \par \uc2  However, sterling was mired against the yen falling to 170 on Tuesday, its lowest since September 1996, down more five percent from Monday's 180.12 high. \par \par \uc2  "Whereas elsewhere sterling has been performing exceptionally well, it has collapsed against the yen and that would tend to reinforce the view that investors are looking for something to buy the yen against," said Coleman at CIBC. "If investors want to load up on yen, maybe for speculative reasons, it just takes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries and the dollar out of the equation." \par \par \uc2  ((London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9e00nw4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
