\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen bulls hold upper hand. \b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 10:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 14 (Reuters) - Yen bulls held the upper hand in early European trading on Tuesday as the market quickly shrugged off the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's dollar buying - which appeared much less aggressive than its ill-fated June/July \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - was no match for the overwhelming capital flows into \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to growing optimism over an economic recovery there, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "I think the pressure for a higher yen is still there because the international benchmark for investors have a tremendous problem here with the strong performance of yen assets," said Michael Rottmann, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich. "They are still forced to reduce their underweightings in yen." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 106.16/21 yen at 0714 GMT, down more than a yen from an overnight high of 107.21 set in the wake of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and within a quarter yen of three-year lows around 106.00 tested in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 109.97/10 yen, down from an overnight high of 111.39 yen and about a half yen off Monday's 109.53 life low. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said overnight that Tokyo had no choice but to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen moved drastically - and that the latest yen rise was "rapid". \par \par \uc2  The comment appeared to confirm suspicion in the market that Japanese authorities were now just trying to smooth the yen's rise, not necessarily reverse it, although some traders still speculated the BOJ could be trying to defend a key chart level in the mid-105-yen area. \par \par \uc2  That level represented a 61.8-percent Fibonacci retracement level of the dollar's rise to 1998 peaks above 147 yen from 1995 lows below 80 yen. \par \par \uc2  "In the end, it's a very tough job for them to defend specific levels without any help from the ECB (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and (U.S. Treasury Secretary) Larry Summers," Rottmann said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa denied \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would table the issue of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when he meets his Group of Seven counterparts later this month, saying the yen's strength was Japan's problem. \par \par \uc2  The euro was slightly softer against the dollar, its sentiment dented by a sharp selloff on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar was last trading at $1.0345/49 against $1.0385/90 late in Europe on Monday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a Japanese bank in London noted the skew in option prices was gradually moving away from a euro-bullish pattern as the market became more wary of the risk the euro would eventually test parity, or $1.00. \par \par \uc2  Euro calls - the right to buy euros for dollars at a pre-set strike price - were giving up premium they had commanded for months over equivalent euro puts - the right to sell euros, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Parity doesn't look very far. It's certainly closer than $1.0830 (early August highs)," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market was awaiting August producer price data for the 11 euro member countries due out at 1000 GMT as well as U.S. retail sales and current account figures later in the day. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9e00njk\par }\page {