\par\par \b \uc2  Japan must consider  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  measures-EPA's Sakaiya. \b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 04:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 14 (Reuters) - Japanese Economic Planning Agency (EPA) Minister Taichi Sakaiya said on Tuesday the government must consider strong measures in response to rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  Sakaiya told a regular news conference, "The yen's rise since Monday has been very rapid and we are watching its movements very carefully." \par \par \uc2  He added that the yen's rise partly reflects confidence in Japan's economic recovery. "The government must consider steadfast measures against (excessively rapid) \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements," he said. \par \par \uc2  Soon after he spoke, the dollar rose sharply over market talk of a fresh round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Regarding so-called "unsterilised" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a form of a credit easing in which yen sold in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is not absorbed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sakaiya said, "In principle, (the BOJ) supplying funds to the money market and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should be considered separately." \par \par \uc2  He added, however, that unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained one option for the BOJ if monetary easing and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were needed at the same time. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next economic package would make reference to monetary policy, Sakaiya said, "I cannot say with certainty, but we will discuss monetary policy as one aspect of our economic measures." \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9e00ne4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
