\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr easier vs yen, BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 operation \highlight\uc2  disappoints some. \b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 1999\par 03:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The dollar eased versus the yen in early Tokyo on Tuesday, weighed down by continued selling by Japanese and overseas banks. \par \par \uc2  No sign of any further credit easing shown in the Bank of Japan's (BOJ) money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday morning also led some dealers to unwind dollar longs. \par \par \uc2  There had been some speculation the BOJ might leave the excess funds in the market in order to conduct a further "quantitative easing" of monetary policy. Tuesday is the settlement day for BOJ's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 106.54/59 yen at 0028 GMT against 106.64/72 yen in late New York on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "There were some speculative dollar longs built up ahead of the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These needed to be unwound," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ left the money market with an estimated surplus of 1.2 trillion yen at its regular 0020 GMT \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a BOJ official told Reuters the cental bank raised the money market surplus from the previous day's surplus of 1.0 trillion yen, based on conditions in the interbank call market on Monday afternoon and Tuesday morning. \par \par \uc2  Despite calls for further credit easing steps by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from rising, BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said in a news conference on Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to continue sterilising \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by draining excess yen funds from the Tokyo money market. \par \par \uc2  Former Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara is one critic of the BOJ's policy. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara, who stepped down as a MOF adviser last week, said on Sunday that the BOJ should cooperate with MOF to stop an excessive rise in the yen through a further easing of its monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in Asian trade, the dollar briefly rose as high as 106.88 yen on buybacks after sales on Monday sent the dollar tumbling nearly three percent against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as low as 106.10 yen in New York on Monday, the lowest level since May 1996, with selling momentum was accelerated by a comment by a White House official suggesting no joint \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  action is likely between Japan and the United States, traders said. \par \par \uc2  White House aide Gene Sperling who attended the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum in New Zealand on Monday denied rumours that the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  planned to coordinate yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a Group of Seven (G7) meeting. \par \par \uc2  "Those rumours were not true. There were never such intentions or plans," Sperling said at a news conference on the sidelines of the APEC meetings. \par \par \uc2  G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors are due to meet in Washington later this month. \par \par \uc2  But caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ and the euro's steady recovery from a historic low versus the yen provided support for the dollar in early Tokyo trade, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "It seems the selling peak of the euro ended when the euro fell below 110 yen," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell to 109.75 yen overnight, a fresh record low, mainly due to selling by Japanese institutional investors, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The euro's fall below 110 yen extended its retreat to more than 15 percent from its level when Japanese corporations closed their books for 1998/99 at the end of March. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 110.74/88 yen at 0100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro was at $1.0402/10, compared with $1.0421/29 in late New York on Monday. The euro dipped below $1.03 overnight for the first time since it flirted with dollar parity in July before bouncing back up. \par \par \uc2  ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.news room@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9e00mte\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
