\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Watch: BOJ Quashes Unsterilized  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Hopes \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum \par \uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 12:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--In an effort to quash hopes that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might leave excess yen sold during \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market, BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said Monday such a policy move wouldn't be effective in easing monetary conditions. \par \par \uc2  Instead, Hayami said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sop up the funds from Friday's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a standard process known as sterilizing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We have continually sterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Because we have provided ample funds to the market (in other ways), it's okay if we handle (Friday's) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the usual way," Hayami said at a regular news conference Monday. \par \par \uc2  Even if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't sterilize the yen sold during Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there would be "little impact" on monetary conditions, he added. \par \par \uc2  The remarks underlined the BOJ's opposition to the controversial idea espoused by some analysts of easing monetary conditions by not draining \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds. \par \par \uc2  They also probably represented a rebuttal against former Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara, who suggested in a television appearance Sunday that the BOJ should consider further steps to keep the yen from rising. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday on behalf of the Finance Ministry in an effort to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but despite buying an estimated $3 billion to $4 billion in the effort, the dollar drifted lower after touching an intraday high at Y109.99. \par \par \uc2  As recently as mid-July, the dollar was trading above Y120. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Partly in reaction to Hayami's comments Monday, the dollar sank below\par its level last week when the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Around 1030 GMT,\par the dollar was quoted at Y106.83.\par -\par     Hayami Warns Against Excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Movements\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions settle two days after deals are made in\par the market, a decision by the BOJ not to sterilize Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par would show up as a rise in the money market's excess banking reserves\par Tuesday morning.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players have grown more confident in recent months\par that the BOJ will continue to sterilize \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and the comments\par Monday didn't represent a policy shift.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nevertheless, Hayami's de facto declaration that the BOJ would\par sterilize on Tuesday was significant because the BOJ doesn't usually\par telegraph its policy intentions so clearly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The comments were also notable because they came amid other remarks in\par which the central banker warned further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be in the\par works.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is possible when (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) moves are sharp,"\par Hayami said at the news conference. "Excessive moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par will have undesirable effects on the economy and prices."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier Monday, the BOJ issued a monthly report that made the point\par more bluntly: "It seems that the recent appreciation of the yen will\par have an adverse effect on corporate profits."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Japan will have trouble pulling the yen back down if the BOJ is\par unwilling to take the radical step of leaving \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds\par unsterilized in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players generally feel Japan hasn't secured its\par trading partners' agreement to conduct joint yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par which the market agrees would be the only sure-fire way of stopping the\par yen from rising further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indeed, even Hayami conceded that Japan would be unable to manipulate\par the dollar-yen rate much without foreign help.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Discussion is needed with other countries to bring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rates to a specific level. Japan alone can't do that," he said.\par    -By Kenneth McCallum; 813-5255-2938; kmccallum@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1030GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1042 4131 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9d06q3f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichg