\par\par \b \uc2  Euro/New Low Vs Yen -3:Dlr Under Y107.30, 3-Yr Low Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 11:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The euro's new low against the yen is well below the Deutsche mark's historic low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reached in April 1995 when it traded as low as Y57.55. That level translates into roughly Y112.55, a level the euro fell through overnight. \par \par \uc2  The dollar crashed through three-year lows against the yen as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged on buying in euro-yen markets. \par \par \uc2  At 0920 GMT, the dollar was at Y107.22, down from Y108.15 late in Asia and Y108.16 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  While London traders are still worried about the possibility of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that fear was mitigated somewhat early Monday by official comments. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi made comments interpreted by markets as opening the door to a stronger yen early Monday. And a U.S. official discounted the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk by finance ministers meeting from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations later this week. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that a midweek bank holiday in Japan on Wednesday may also be contributing to a growing feeling in Europe that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It certainly isn't going to happen this week," said one London-based trader. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0930GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9d06py