\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW/Utsumi -2: In Constant Contact With US On  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 06:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The speed of the yen's recent rise versus the dollar has been excessive, given the fragility of Japan's economic recovery, said Keio University professor Makoto Utsumi Monday. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Dow Jones Newswires, Utsumi also said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the dollar last Friday was appropriate. \par \par \uc2  "It was very reasonable for Japanese monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of last week. They'll do their best to prevent an excessive yen rise versus the dollar from hitting Japan's fragile economic recovery," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  A former vice minister for international affairs at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Utsumi said that Japanese monetary authorities are carefully watching whether Japan's economic recovery is sustainable in light of current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  Although Utsumi noted that Japanese monetary authorities don't necessarily have a specific \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level in mind as a target, he said: "Still, they might think yen strength (against the dollar) that exceeds Y110 at this moment is potentially dangerous." \par \par \uc2  When asked what an appropriate range for the dollar-yen would be, Utsumi said, "In my view, it is between Y110 and Y120." He added that Japanese monetary authorities would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi also said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been in constant contact with U.S. monetary authorities on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and that Washington understands Tokyo's stance on the yen. \par \par \uc2  "I have no doubt that Japan has gotten the U.S.'s understanding regarding its solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There is no U.S. disagreement on what \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is doing," Utsumi said. \par \par \uc2  When asked whether U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible, he said: "The U.S. would not do that (joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) for the sake of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If the U.S. does that, it would do it for the sake of its own country." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0403GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9d06pbq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
