\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ may have  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  via BOE on Friday-bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 11:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 13 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) may have bought dollars against the yen through the Bank of England (BOE) in early European trade last Friday, bankers said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  They said the BOE had been detected purchasing on behalf of the BOJ through several Japanese commercial banks and European banks when the dollar edged below 109 yen in early European market trading hours on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The BOE was initially detected to have bought through an electronic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage system and it later bought directly through the banks, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOE may have bought through several Japanese and European banks (on Friday) on behalf of the BOJ when the dollar fell to around 108.50/60 yen," one banker said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar jumped by about one yen to around 109.50 yen following the action in the European markets," the banker said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Friday, the dollar surged to as high as 110.00 yen from a low of 107.65 yen following BOJ yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was estimated to have spent about $2 billion in Friday's Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its first dollar-buying foray since July 21, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as the agent of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the dollar was back under under pressure against the yen, but there was no trace of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0906 GMT, the dollar was at 107.44/49 yen against 108.69/79 yen in New York late on Friday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9d00tra\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
