\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar falls to three-year lows against yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 11:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 13 (Reuters) - The dollar extended recent losses and fell to three-year lows below 107.50 yen against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday amid growing optimism over an economic recovery in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday also encouraged yen bulls to keep pushing the yen higher, particularly since Friday's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have much lasting effect, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as low as 107.10 yen by 0915 GMT, down from 108.80/85 yen late in Europe on Friday. A flurry of stop-loss selling was triggered as the dollar broke through the 107.50-yen level, accelerating the decline. \par \par \uc2  The bullish outlook for the Japanese economy prompted overseas investors to shift more investment into Japanese equities, in which they had been underweight for many years, traders said. Japanese investors, meanwhile, were being forced to hedge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses on, or in some cases even liquidate, their foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  Such investor activity earlier led the euro to fall below 111 yen for the first time since its launch in January. Traders said heavy euro/yen selling also helped drag down the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Next major target for dollar/yen was seen in the mid-105-yen area, the 61.8 percent Fibonacci retracement of the dollar's rise to October 1998 peaks above 147 yen from its 1995 troughs below 80 yen. ((London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \p