\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen buoyant amid BOJ absence. \b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 13 (Reuters) - The yen remained buoyant in Europe on Monday, bumping against lifetime highs against the euro set overnight, amid growing optimism over an economic pickup in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen's positive momentum had accelerated after a surprise increase in Japan's second quarter growth data last week, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday was woefully insufficient to curb the yen's strength, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "They did try to sell it (Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) as a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than sort of a line in the sand, but...either \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  works or it doesn't," said Francis Breedon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Lehman Brothers in London. "At the moment, it seems it doesn't. So they do need to do something more serious the next time around." \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at 111.95/15 yen at 0728 GMT against 113.60/79 late in Europe on Friday. It fell below 112 yen earlier in the session for the first time since the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was launched in January. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 108.01/11 yen against 108.80/85 late on Friday and last week's three-year low of 107.52. \par \par \uc2  Although no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been detected so far today, BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said in Tokyo that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible when \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were moving too rapidly, although the BOJ needed to consult other central banks in order to change the market's direction and guide the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to certain levels." \par \par \uc2  Hayami also remarked that the yen's recent rise had been "a bit rapid". \par \par \uc2  Traders said that short of coordinated international \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a de-facto BOJ credit easing through so-called unsterlised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be the only card the Japanese authorities had at the moment to halt the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Hayami, however, rejected that option. \par \par \uc2  He said the BOJ planned to keep sterilising its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - meaning it would drain excess liquidity in the private sector banking system resulting from its dollar buying for yen. \par \par \uc2  "Some people had bought dollars in Tokyo in anticipation of some BOJ action, but they seem to have become frustrated and are liquidating now," said a dealer at a Japanese bank in London. "If we don't see any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market will probably target stops under 107.70 yen." \par \par \uc2  The euro was broadly under pressure after German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's Social Democrats suffered another heavy defeat in a state election on Sunday, a setback for the government's effort to push through its austerity programme. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar was last trading at $1.0350/55 against $1.0445/50 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the preliminary second quarter gross domestic product data for the 11 euro-member countries due out at 1000 GMT could be key for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's near-term direction. Economists polled by Reuters have, on average, forecast a rise of 0.4 percent for the Q2 GDP. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese bank dealer said the dollar's rally above key chart points against the Swiss franc boded ill for the euro. \par \par \uc2  The dollar broke above late-August highs in the 1.54-franc area on Friday, triggering a flurry of short-covering, and was last trading at 1.5540/50 francs. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9d00tbe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
