\par\par \b \uc2  Confident yen shrugs off  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat. \b0\par\par\uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 13 (Reuters) - The yen overcame early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters on Monday to grab a bagful of gains on the dollar and a fresh lifetime high against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The dollar did briefly rise to 109.20 yen in early trade as the market feared the reappearance of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) after Friday's two billion dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  But as the morning dragged on, the sellers came out of hiding and the dollar had slid to 108.36/41 yen by 0330 GMT against 108.69/79 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro was in even worse shape, barely managing to top 113.00 yen before crumbling to a new trough at 112.35, leaving dealers confidently expecting 110.00 before the week's end. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted these were significant levels for euro/yen since 112.45 corresponded to the all-time low for mark/yen of around 57.55 yen, hit in April 1995. \par \par \uc2  "We've been watching this level for a while," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "If it cracks, which you have to say is certain, there'll be nothing but vacuum beneath the euro," he said, predicting a fall to at least 107.00 in the short to medium term. \par \par \uc2  He was equally bearish on dollar/yen given the brevity of its bounce this morning and the following breach of support around 108.40 yen. \par \par \uc2  "As soon as it got above 109.00 the sell orders started to come in; we never got a chance to fill the exporter offers around 109.50," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The only thing keeping the dollar up is the threat of the BOJ, but even that's only good for this time zone," he added, noting that the BOJ did not act during European and New York hours on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers thought it only a matter of time before last week's three-year low at 107.55 yen was tested and analysts were looking for a fall to 105.65 - a 62 percent retracement of the dollar's entire uptrend from 79.70 in April 1995 to last year's peak at 147.63. \par \par \uc2  There was some speculation the BOJ would reinforce its opposition to the yen's rise by leaving its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised when Friday's dollar purchases are settled on Tuesday. The BOJ sterilised all its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and July by draining the excess funds out of the money market. Leaving the excess in the market would be seen as making monetary policy even easier and would provide at least symbolic support for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said all the signs from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were that it did not believe unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was necessary or even effective. \par \par \uc2  They expected BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami to stick to that stance when he gives a regular news conference at 0600 GMT on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, had lost out to the dollar after U.S. asset markets ended the week on a resilient note. Bond prices and the NASDAQ stock index gained when a surprise 0.1 percent dip in core producer prices lessened the risk of a Federal Reserve tightening at its next meeting in October. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the euro was also burdened by another poor showing in local elections over the weekend from German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's ruling Social Democrats. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the setback will make it harder for Schroeder to push through promised austerity measures which the market favoured. \par \par \uc2  The euro was languishing at $1.0371/76, having sunk to $1.0365 in New York from $1.0530 late here on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the process it snapped trendline support around $1.0525 and breached an important retracement target at $1.0380, which left technical analysts tipping a retreat to the next major bulwark at $1.0280. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also made hefty gains on the Swiss franc, with traders reporting heavy options-related and technical buying on Friday following the break of resistance above 1.5200 francs which saw it jump to a two-month high of 1.5520 \par \par \uc2  The dollar was holding at 1.5490/00 in Tokyo and dealers looked for a push towards its July highs in the 1.5865/90 area. \par \par \uc2  ((Wayne Cole, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8584 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9d00sse\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
