\par\par \b \uc2  US denies G7 plans to discuss  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  AUCKLAND, Sept 13 (Reuters) - A White House official on Monday denied rumours that the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had planned to coordinate yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the upcoming Group of Seven (G7) meeting. \par \par \uc2  "Those rumours were not true. There were never such intentions or plans," White House aide Gene Sperling said in response to a question at a news conference on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum in New Zealand. \par \par \uc2  The Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors are due to meet in Washington later this month. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by selling yen for dollars in an attempt to halt the recent rise of the yen, which Tokyo fears could undermine the country's frail economic recovery by making its exports more expensive abroad. \par \par \uc2  Japan has said it does not expect \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be specifically discussed at the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9d00srl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
