\par\par \b \uc2  Hayami - BOJ to keep sterilising  \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 13 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami said on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to "sterilise" its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by draining excess yen funds from the Tokyo money market. \par \par \uc2  "We are already providing ample funding through other means," Hayami told a regular news conference when asked about calls for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop sterilising its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to weaken the yen and provide further monetary easing. \par \par \uc2  "I have fully discussed this with authorities overseas and received their understanding," he added. \par \par \uc2  Hayami reiterated the BOJ's doubts about whether an unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be effective than the present monetary policy of pumping funds into the market to guide the key overnight interest rate essentially to zero. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sterilise Friday's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when settlements are made on Tuesday, Hayami said, "We are providing ample funds and so this will be a normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  He said other central banks also routinely sterilise their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hayami reiterated that the BOJ will maintain its zero interest rate policy until an end to deflation fears is in sight. He added that deflationary fears remain as downward pressure on prices persists. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said Japanese financial institutions were making steady progress in preparing to deal with Y2K computer glitches. \par \par \uc2  This was fundamentally the responsibility of the banks but "the Bank of Japan is watching the situation closely and will act as needed" to deal with any problems. \par \par \uc2  Asked about concern over possible massive outflows from the postal savings system when high-yielding deposits mature over the next two years, Hayami said he did not anticipate any major problems at the moment. \par \par \uc2  He acknowledged that it was difficult to estimate at this stage what any net outflows may amount to, and said the BOJ will remain in close contact with the government on the issue. \par \par \uc2  ((Billy Mallard, Tokyo Economic Policy Desk +81-3 5473-3748 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9d00n2h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
