\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Yen shrugs off post- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  lows. \b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Broad-based yen strength may have been temporarily stalled by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight on Thursday, but unless dollar/yen rises above 111, yen strength is expected to resurface. \par \par \uc2  The yen regained around one yen in early Europe after being knocked down more two percent against the dollar following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ to sell yen for dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ have acted to put a floor on dollar/yen, but they are going to have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in order to push the floor any higher than we are now," said Tony Norfield, head of global treasury research at ABN AMRO. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was at 109.01/11 by 0727 GMT compared with a high set overnight at 109.97 and a three-year low set on Thursday at 107.52. \par \par \uc2  Norfield said trendline resistance around 110.50/111 coupled with the overnight high suggested 110 would be a tough barrier. \par \par \uc2  "The (BOJ) would need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push it up to 111 and above in order to properly neutralise this negative sentiment on dollar/yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was confirmed by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. He said the movements in dollar/yen had been violent and that Japan's consumption and capital expenditure still needed support from government steps. Miyazawa also said the yen's rise was Japan's problem. \par \par \uc2  "Miyazawa made it relatively clear that it is too early to say the recovery is self sustaining, so maybe over-optimism about the Japanese recovery will moderate now," said Eugen Keller, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt, adding this might limit the downside for dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen's moves against the dollar have been reflected by those seen against the euro. Euro/yen was last at 114.97/115.07, off an overnight high of 115.70, but up more than one percent from a life low at 113.26 set on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "After a number of weeks when the (Japanese authorities) seemed to indicate they probably would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the U.S. joined in, the rapidity of the latest yen moves not only against the dollar, but also against the euro, makes them see it more as a yen problem," said Norfield at ABN. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, analysts said the short-term outlook for euro/dollar was soft. The euro was last at $1.0519/23 after reaching $1.0486 overnight, its lowest in nearly two weeks. \par \par \uc2  "The techincal situtation has worsened since yesterday as a few speculators bet on an early rate hike by the ECB and took (the decision) as a disappoiontment selling euro heavily against sterling and the dollar," said Keller at Dresdner. \par \par \uc2  "The euro faces some pressure short-term. If we close below 1.0525 it would be relatively negative and could lead to a further downside bias towards 1.0440 and 1.0400." \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  voted to keep the euro zone refinancing rate at 2.50 percent on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  ECB President Wim Duisenberg said after the decision was announced that a tightening bias continued to creep into the ECB's thinking, but at a "snail's pace". \par \par \uc2  Keller said Duisenberg's comments suggested it might be quite some time before the ECB followed its British and U.S. counterparts in raising interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "Overall this has led to some disappointment that we will probably have to wait a bit longer for a rate hike and this will weigh on the euro," he said. \par \par \uc2  ABN's Norfield said activity in yen could impact euro/dollar making sterling an attractive alternative for investors. \par \par \uc2  "Sterling against the euro and the dollar is a safer play and that is one of the reasons we are seeing sterling firm again against the euro and remaining pretty firm on the cable rate as well," he said. \par \par \uc2  The pound was last at $1.6326/36 within half a cent of the $1.6374 four-month peak hit on Thursday. Euro/sterling was at 64.41/43 within sight of a three-month low at 64.32 set earlier. ((Deepthi Wickremasinghe, London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00zaz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
