\par\par \b \uc2  Nikkei struggles higher, blunted by yen worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 09:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Tokyo's key Nikkei average edged up on Friday, as growing confidence in Japan's economy marginally offset worries about the strong yen, which lingered despite dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei average of 225 leading shares closed up 33.46 points or 0.19 percent at 17,711.02. But Nikkei December futures ended 50 points lower at 17,690. \par \par \uc2  Japan's positive gross domestic product data for the April-June period released on Thursday prompted investors to buy into sectors that may benefit from an economic recovery, such as construction and telecoms. \par \par \uc2  Companies seen moving ahead with restructuring moves to improve efficiency also drew attention, with NEC Corp  soaring 239 yen or 12.44 percent to 2,160 in the heaviest trading volume in the Tokyo bourse's first section. \par \par \uc2  It briefly rose as high as 2,175, a high for this year. \par \par \uc2  A business daily reported on Friday the company would post a 100 billion yen special loss in 1999/2000 from broad restructuring steps. \par \par \uc2  But market participants remained cautious over volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stifle the yen's strength sent the dollar surging to 110 yen from early levels below 108. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar failed to take advantage of the BOJ's help, and was trading back down below 109 yen in late Tokyo afternoon trade. The prospect of further yen strength weighed on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -sensitive exporters such as auto makers, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Without a big positive surprise, the stock market was not able to test higher levels," said Mamoru Shimode, a strategist at Deutsche Securities Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Export-oriented manufacturers, whose overseas profits are reduced by a rising yen, fared poorly. \par \par \uc2  Toyota Motor Corp  declined 70 yen or 2.02 percent to 3,400 and Honda Motor Co Ltd  slipped 40 yen or 0.84 percent to 4,700. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to a fresh three-year low of 107.55 yen overnight in New York, following the relatively healthy 0.2 percent growth in Japan's GDP for April-June released on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Trading is a bit slow ahead of the weekend. People are also guarded due to the yen's fluctuations," said Hiroichi Nishi, deputy general manager at Nikko Securities Co Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Top Japanese government spokesman Hiromu Nonaka said on Friday there was concern that a sudden rise in the yen could have negative impact on Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "We do not believe this is desirable. There is no fundamental change in our stance on this," he told a regular news conference. \par \par \uc2  On the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange, a total of 1.17 billion shares changed hands, up from 473.99 million on Thursday, inflated by trading related to the settlement of September futures and options on the Nikkei 225 stock average. \par \par \uc2  The Osaka Securities Exchange announced on Friday that the special quotation (SQ) for the settlement was 17,517.17 points. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On broader indices, the TOPIX index\tab    of all first-section shares edged up 7.24 points or 0.48 percent to 1,514.86, while the Nikkei 300 \tab  was up 0.42 point or 0.14 percent at 296.15.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Decliners outpaced advancers 658 to 565, while 120 issues were unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stock indices for smaller capitalised stocks outperformed those for first section stocks, with the second section index\tab    surging 54.68 points or 2.10 percent to 2,659.09 and the over-the-counter (OTC) market index\tab    jumping 43.94 points or 2.21 percent to 2,036.28.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The OTC topped the 2,000-point level on Friday for the first time since July 1994.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Construction firms rose, with Obayashi Corp  up 23 yen or 3.54 percent to 672 and major home builder Sekisui House Ltd  up 42 yen or 3.6 percent at 1,210.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Telecommunications remained bullish, with NTT Mobile Communications Network Inc (NTT Docomo)  up 60,000 yen or 3.11 percent at 1.99 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said earnings of these companies were immune to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuations. Elsewhere, Kirin Brewery Co Ltd  climbed 78 yen or 6.13 percent to 1,350.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The beer and drinks maker said on Friday it would hold a news conference at 4 p.m. (0700 GMT) on reorganisation of its group companies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Tokyo Equities Desk +81-3 5473 3714 tokyo.equities.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00z0v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
