\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS - Euro up vs yen after BOJ lifts dlr/yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 04:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The euro was sharply higher against the yen in late morning Tokyo on Friday, in tandem with a jump in the dollar/yen rate set off by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the euro also received a boost against the yen on a large-lot buying, which was seen as Japanese corporate demand for euro. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 115.52/60 yen at 0151 GMT, compared with 113.80 yen in New York late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yen had risen to a three-year high of 107.55 yen to the dollar and a lifetime high of 113.02 yen against the euro overnight, buoyed by Thursday's Japanese gross domestic product (GDP) data showing a stronger-than-expected 0.2 percent growth. \par \par \uc2  "Large-lot buying of euro for yen was detected in early trade before there was any talk of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . According to market talk, a Japanese corporation was behind that trade," said a dealer at a Japanese commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the purpose of the firm's euro buying was unknown. \par \par \uc2  The euro then extended gains in line with the dollar, which surged over two yen to 109.77 yen from an earlier low of 107.65 after BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars around 109 yen, its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the yen's rise since July 21. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was later confirmed by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and the Finance Ministry's International Bureau chief Zembei Mizoguchi. \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected that Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed mainly at giving Japanese exporters a chance to sell more dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The government must be more confident about the economy after a solid GDP data. So the current dollar/yen rate itself is probably not that worrisome for the government," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Swiss franc was at 72.29/34 yen, compared with 71.06 yen in New York late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at 179.05/17 yen versus 176.55 yen in New York. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-1396, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00yle\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
