\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr surges as BOJ steps in to curb yen strength. \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 03:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The dollar leapt against the yen in early Tokyo trade on Friday, after the Bank of Japan (BOJ) stepped into the market to sell yen for dollars, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars around 109 yen, its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the yen's rise since July 21. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's action lifted the greenback nearly two yen to around 109.50 yen from an earlier low of 107.65 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 109.39/44 yen at 0045 GMT, compared with 108.00/10 yen in New York late on Thursday. The euro was at $1.0539/41, steady from $1.0530/35 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had fallen as low as 107.55 yen overnight in New York, its lowest level since August 27, 1996. \par \par \uc2  "After yesterday's strong Japan GDP data, the market was set to push the yen further up in Tokyo this morning," said a trust bank dealer. "But people rushed to square dollar shorts after talk spread that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars." \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa later confirmed that the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at slowing the yen's rise, not an attempt to forcibly move dollar/yen levels higher. \par \par \uc2  The dollar later extended its gains to 109.77 yen, after more Japanese officials confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken appropriate action on Friday against rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said selling interest by Japanese exporters and investors was likely to cap the dollar around 110 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is probably aimed at rescuing exporters and investors. I don't think the current dollar/yen level itself is that worrisome for authorities as Tokyo stocks are looking resilient despite the yen rise," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei 225 average was up 0.63 percent at 17,789.20 as of 0118 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 115.15/22 yen, up sharply from 113.80 yen in New York late on Thursday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00yjw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
