\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2  to check yen rally. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 09:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the sagging dollar against the yen on Friday for the first time since July 21. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted, however, that the "style" and amount of its dollar purchases were clearly different from a few months ago. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to buy dollars for yen in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  Bankers estimated the BOJ spent approximately $2 billion - much less than in its aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and July. \par \par \uc2  Market activity was thin when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first tapped it with bids on the dollar, maximising the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and exaggerating the dollar's upward swing. \par \par \uc2  The dollar shot up to 110.00 yen by late morning from Tokyo's early low of 107.65 yen. The greenback had dived overnight to a three-year low of 107.55 yen after Japan announced stronger than expected second-quarter gross domestic product data on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Koji Fukaya, chief analyst at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Treasury Division of Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said the BOJ's dollar purchases could be defined as a "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". \par \par \uc2  "The authorities appear to have no intention to drive up the dollar forcefully as they did in June and July," he said. \par \par \uc2  It was more aimed at making some opportunity for pent-up dollar sales demand to be exhausted in the market, he added. \par \par \uc2  "There's not much point in depressing the yen's value in light of more signs of economic recovery and capital flows favouring the yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  Takeshi Hanai, executive manager of the International Treasury Department at the Industrial Bank of Japan, said: "With dollar purchases today, the BOJ is simply giving exporters a chance to sell the dollar. I don't think there was any hidden, greater ambition behind the BOJ's move." \par \par \uc2  Local exporters have not yet sold as many dollars as their commercial needs warrant, bankers said. They had to convert dollars into yen to settle export profits in yen terms. \par \par \uc2  In June and July, the BOJ spent an estimated $37.76 billion in an aggressive bid to jack up the level of dollar against the yen. The BOJ acts as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's agent in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Former Vice Finance Minister of International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara was still in office and directing the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to early July. \par \par \uc2  He was succeeded by Haruhiko Kuroda, who is known in the market as a scholarly type of administrator who has little desire to do anything beyond what is logically feasible. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Japanese authorities would neither chase the dollar above 110 yen nor try to change its bearish trend against the yen as they are aware that the yen's strength is based on changed expectations on the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  But they would only check the speed of the yen's appreciation, they added. \par \par \uc2  Japan registered surprise economic growth in April-June after a stunning rise in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  The government said on Thursday that gross domestic product, the value of all goods and services, rise an inflation-adjusted 0.2 percent in April-June, or an annualised 0.9 percent, which was at the top of economists' forecasts. \par \par \uc2  "The main message from the policy-makers is that they're opposed to a rapid movement," said Ken Landon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa on Friday: "We will move to correct violent movements (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)." \par \par \uc2  But Miyazawa also said in a recent interview with a local daily that it was inevitable Japan's economic recovery would be gradually reflected in the markets. \par \par \uc2  Capital flows also favour yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry data shows that Japanese have turned net sellers of U.S. bonds since the fourth quarter of 1998, unloading 453.9 billion yen ($4.13 billion) on an annualised basis. \par \par \uc2  Japanese had been net buyers of an annualised 3 trillion yen from the first quarter 1995 to the third quarter of 1998. \par \par \uc2  ($1=110 yen) ((Yoshiko Mori, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8676 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00ux3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
