\par\par \b \uc2  Sickly dollar heads for 100 yen despite BOJ help. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wayne Cole \par \uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 08:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The dollar is locked in a bear trend which could yet see one cent equal one yen, despite an eyebrow-raising rally on Friday. \par \par \uc2  For one thing the bounce was all the work of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with no real institutional flows behind it. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , alarmed by the dollar's dive to three-year lows overnight, stepped in to buy around 107.70/80 yen and squeezed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a high of 110.00. \par \par \uc2  But the jump fizzled there after completing a 62 percent retracement of the week's fall from 111.40 to 107.55, leaving the dollar to drift back to 109.34/39 in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the rise repaired a little of the damage done by the break of 108.70 support on Thursday but could not patch over the fact that the January lows around 108.20 had been breached. \par \par \uc2  "The key point is, we've had a much-tested level, this 108.20/70 level which had held all year, and it's clearly been broken," Peter Pontikas, technical analyst at Westpac Bank in Sydney, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "We're in a dollar-bear market and it's got further to run. It seems like 105.00 is a reasonable bet in the next few weeks and we must start to entertain the prospect of 100.00 very soon." \par \par \uc2  At that level there would be an argument that the dollar offered good value for the medium term, "but as with all these things we must get to a stage where it's undervalued," he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted the dollar rally had stopped well short of the 110.70/80 yen level held Thursday before upbeat Japanese economic growth data sent it spiraling lower. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also failed to clear the top of a downtrend channel which has been guiding it down since early July when it was up at 123.00 yen. This currently comes in around 110.70, making this an important resistance level in the short term. \par \par \uc2  The week's high point at 111.40 was also considered a key level with many arguing that the dollar needed a New York close above that to really turn the bearish tide. \par \par \uc2  Without it, they looked for a break of support around 109.30 to sound an early warning of a fresh slide to support at 108.55, 108.10 and the 107.55 low. \par \par \uc2  Beyond there the target remained 105.65, which would be a 62 percent retracement of the entire uptrend from the record trough of 79.70 in April 1995 to last year's peak at 147.63. Some also divined ominous signs for the dollar on the weekly charts since it had snapped the neckline of a massive head and shoulders formation which stretches all the way back to January 1997. \par \par \uc2  In this case a break below January's trough around 108.20 would complete the second shoulder and signal the start of a bear phase with 100.00 yen as merely the first target. \par \par \uc2  If it goes by the textbook, the destination on the downside would equal the distance from the neckline to the top of the head, which in this case is 37 yen, throwing up a long-term target of no less than 73 yen. ((Wayne Cole, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8584 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00uuv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
