\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ estimated to have spent $2bln in market on Fri. \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 07:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan was estimated to have spent approximately $2 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday in Tokyo to check the yen's swift advance, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Market activity was thin when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first tapped it with bids on the dollar, maximising the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and exaggerating the dollar's upward swing, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  "Given the BOJ placed its dollar purchase orders several times at major U.S. and European investment banks and some Japanese city banks, the amount could have totalled $2 billion," one Japanese banker said. \par \par \uc2  The volume was much smaller compared with the BOJ's dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and July, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Friday's BOJ's dollar purchases was its first since July 21. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as agent of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on Friday in Tokyo, saying that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had been "violent," adding that Japan would try to correct such moves. \par \par \uc2  Helped by the BOJ, the dollar surged to 110.00 yen by late morning trading from Tokyo's early low of 107.65 yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen had surged to three-year highs overnight after Japan announced a stronger than expected second quarter gross domestic product (GDP) figure on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  ((Yoshiko Mori, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8676 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00uu7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
