\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar claws back ground after  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 16:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The dollar started the U.S. day at higher levels after Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars in the open market overnight, helping rescue the greenback from the three-year lows it had hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese officials said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had swooped into the market during Asian trading to help quell the yen's recent sharp gains, sparked by fresh hopes that Japan is finally pulling out of its worst postwar recession. \par \par \uc2  News Japan's gross domestic product had grown 0.2 percent in the April to June quarter, defying forecasts for a contraction, had sent the yen up more than three percent against the dollar and Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The data soothed some fears that a strong yen could derail Japan's fragile recovery, but overnight a Japanese government spokesman expressed fresh concern about the dangers of an overly strong yen. \par \par \uc2  "We do not believe this is desirable. There is no fundamental change in our stance on this," Hiromu Nonaka told journalists. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders estimated the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about $2 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and predicted there may be more sales during New York trading hours. \par \par \uc2  "Historically speaking there is never just one bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and since the bank has to push dollar/yen above 110 in order to begin changing the market's mind about the yen's direction, I expect we will see them again today," said John Schein, vice president at Generale USA Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  The dollar started New York trading at 109.10/20 yen, more than a full yen above Thursday's 108.00/10 closing level. \par \par \uc2  The greenback also gained ground against Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , approaching two week highs as the euro slipped as low as $1.0460 in early New York trading. The pair had dipped to $1.0513/18 as New York trading got underway from Thursday's $1.0530/35 closing level. \par \par \uc2  Softer than expected U.S. inflation data, possibly reducing the need for another near-term U.S. interest rate hike, helped spark euro sales at a time many dealers remain nervous about the pace of European recovery. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing a lot of customer interest in selling the euro, but it should not be viewed as anything terribly dramatic," a dealer said. Technical analysts said losses to $1.0420 could prompt more sales, leading the euro as low as $1.0225. \par \par \uc2  Sharp gains in energy and raw materials prices helped push August's producer price index up 0.5 percent, but dealers quickly paid more attention to the core rate which contracted 0.1 percent. The core rate strips out volatile food and energy prices. \par \par \uc2  Economists had forecast an overall gain of 0.3 percent following July's 0.2 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  Wall Street also applauded the tame inflation news, sending the Dow Jones industrial average up about 20 points shortly after the opening. Any sustained gains may be helpful for the dollar, dealers agreed. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the dollar also gained against the Swiss franc, rising to 1.5234/45 from 1.5200/10 while the British pound lost ground, slipping to $1.6285/92 from $1.6335/45. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar started modestly softer at $0.6522/32 after $0.6529/34 on Thursday. The dollar rose against the Canadian dollar to C$1.4801/11 from C$1.4776/86. \par \par \uc2  ((-North American Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00r7d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
