\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ indicates will 'sterilise' Friday  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its current stance on money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Friday, indicating it will stick to its practice of "sterilising" a yen surplus resulting from Friday's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday, when the settlement of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls due, the money market is expected to have an extra surplus of over 200 billion yen. \par \par \uc2  But the BOJ official said: "The bank will decide its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on the day's overall supply-demand conditions and levels of the key overnight call market, as usual." \par \par \uc2  The official's remark suggested that the extra surplus caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is most likely to be sterilised. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was estimated to have bought $2 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, meaning the yen the BOJ sold will flood the interbank market on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Until now, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drained such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -generated yen surpluses from the money market through its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But some politicians and economists have urged the BOJ to leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  surplus funds "unsterilised" in the money market as a form of radical "quantitative" monetary easing. ((Tokyo newsroom (813) 3432-8022 Tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00r1b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
