\par\par \b \uc2  TOCOM rubber ends down on profit-taking, firm yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Tokyo rubber futures closed lower on Friday across the board on profit-taking selling and the yen's firmer tone against the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But rubber futures are expected to rise in coming weeks due to expectations stocks will continue to dwindle and concerns about tightening supply from producing countries, they said. \par \par \uc2  Rubber futures ranged from 1.4 to 3.3 yen per kg lower. Benchmark February futures fell 1.4 yen to 75.8. "The loss in today's rubber futures was mainly due to profit-taking selling after rubber futures gained in the past four trading days," said a commodity analyst. The yen's firmer tone against the dollar despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday also weighed on the market, he said. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar was higher against the yen late on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier bought an estimated $2 billion in an effort to halt the yen's surge in value. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 109.05/10 yen as of 0618 GMT, against 108.00/10 yen in New York late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese rubber futures would likely rise further next week on improved market sentiment and may test a resistance of 80 yen for the benchmark February contract, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But they said rubber futures would face profit-taking selling pressure before testing 80 yen, and could also be held back by the yen's advance against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  One trader pegged support for the benchmark contract at 75 yen and 73 yen. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431 tokyo.commodit.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9a00qf5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
