\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar pares gains vs yen in Tokyo, Japan GDP eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 09:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The dollar pared earlier gains against the yen by late Tokyo on Wednesday, after trading in a tight range ahead of the release on Thursday of Japan's April-June gross domestic product (GDP) data. \par \par \uc2  Although dealers' position squaring before the key data release lifted the dollar earlier, the U.S. unit was capped by persistent selling by Japanese exporters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 110.90/95 yen at 0616 GMT, compared with 110.72/82 yen in New York late on Tuesday. It earlier rose as high as 111.10 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0602/07, versus $1.0585/90 in New York. \par \par \uc2  "We may see more stop-loss dollar buying around 111.50 yen, but I doubt the dollar has enough strength to rise above 112 yen," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  "Squaring of short dollar, long yen positions triggered after yesterday's (Japan) corporate survey data seems largely completed. Exporters are also detected selling above 111 yen," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar climbed as high as 111.35 yen overnight after the Japanese Finance Ministry's corporate survey data released on Tuesday showed a 13.4 percent year-on-year drop in corporate capital spending in the April-June quarter. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry data prompted some economists to slightly lower their forecasts for the April-June GDP. \par \par \uc2  The revisions lowered the average forecast of 27 economists polled by Reuters to a contraction of 0.35 percent from the January-March quarter. The same economists had an average forecast of minus 0.3 in a September 1 Reuters survey. The April-June GDP is being closely watched as the government has said the data will be the basis for deciding the size of a promised supplementary budget later this year. \par \par \uc2  "After the GDP release, the market's focus is likely to shift to the size of the extra budget," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Taku Yamasaki, a former policy chief of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party, said on Wednesday that Japan should enact a 10 trillion yen extra budget for the business year to next March 31. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was unmoved by Yamasaki's comments as the market's consensus for the size of the upcoming extra budget fell somewhere between five and 10 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers said they did not expect the yen's uptrend to change after the GDP release, as a small contraction in the April-June GDP was unlikely to cool expectations of a further economic recovery in Japan in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  But dealers were still wary about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June to curb the yen's strength on the day the robust January-March GDP data invited aggressive yen buying. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said the ministry welcomed the dollar's rise overnight above 111 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's appreciation before Japan's economy recovers is not desirable, and it is good that the market understands this," Mizoguchi told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers dismissed talk of dollar-buying by European and Japanese pharmaceutical firms related to a possible settlement of a $1 billion U.S. lawsuit. \par \par \uc2  "There were rumours that such dollar buying may take place today but we have not seen such flows. I think the rumours are overblown," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Washington Post said on Tuesday six vitamin makers had agreed to pay more than $1.1 billion in costs and damage to customers, mainly food and drink manufacturers, stemming from alleged price-fixing. \par \par \uc2  The market also shrugged off news that rating agency Duff & Phelps had changed its outlook on Japanese local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt to negative from stable. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro was higher against the yen amid increasing optimism about the outlook for euro-zone economies. \par \par \uc2  The euro was quoted at 117.93/01 yen as of 0655 GMT against 117.26 yen in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's Policy Board will meet on Thursday but analysts said they expected no fresh policy move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv98012cu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
