\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Stunning sterling dominates dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 17:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The pound galloped ahead against the dollar in Europe on Wednesday after a surprise increase in British interest rates, but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained little changed on the day against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A quarter point rise in the British repo rate to 5.25 percent, making British rates level with the U.S. federal funds target rate, thrust the pound to one-month highs against the dollar, more than two cents above the day's lows. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar held steady against the yen and euro, ahead of keenly-awaited Japanese gross domestic product data due at 2350 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "People are a little wary of taking big positions ahead of that number," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Warburg Dillon Read. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 110.95/98 yen at 1409 GMT, from 110.86/95 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The release in June of data showing unexpectedly strong Japanese GDP growth in the first quarter sparked a series of at least seven yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and July. \par \par \uc2  But Japanese GDP is expected to show a contraction of 0.35 percent in the April-June quarter, according to a Reuters poll released on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The market remains wary that tonight's data could trigger another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's absence from the market since July 21, when the dollar was nine yen stronger. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts were sceptical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take place. \par \par \uc2  "It's unlikely that there will be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the Japanese will come in with a sensible fiscal package, and there is concern about the huge U.S. current account deficit," said David Brickman, senior international economist at PaineWebber. \par \par \uc2  With yen traders' hands tied by the Japanese GDP data, attention switched to the pound and the possibility of further British interest rate rises. \par \par \uc2  "Today's move has come out of the blue and there is no reason to think that this will be the last rate increase we will see this year," said Andrew Milligan, director of economic research at Morley Fund Management in London. \par \par \uc2  "The factors which the bank pointed to are not going to fade dramatically over the next few months and from a fundamental point of view this should push sterling higher." \par \par \uc2  The pound was trading at $1.6198/08 at 1445 GMT, off an earlier high of $1.6261 but up from the day's low at $1.6044 and from $1.6052/62 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro benefited briefly from sterling's rise, amid some speculation the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might follow suit in raising interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The MPC cited world demand as one of the factors behind the British rate rise, which analysts said was also a potential issue for the ECB. \par \par \uc2  But a near-term rise in euro-zone interest rates was unlikely, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The MPC and the ECB are totally different - the MPC cannot stop moving rates, but you would have to get the ECB at gunpoint in a dark alley to get them to move," said Crise. \par \par \uc2  The ECB holds its next fortnightly policy meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was earlier undermined by a 1.0 percent increase in German industrial output in July from June, below expectations. \par \par \uc2  It was trading at $1.0598/02 at 1504 GMT, from the week's high of $1.0644 ahead of the German data and from $1.0583/85 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro fell to 117.47/65 from earlier two-week highs of 118.40, but remained above late Tuesday's 117.26/45. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9800v9i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
